---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import { site } from "../config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sift Support"
  description="Practical scan tips, data guidance, safety boundaries, and answers to common questions about using Sift."
  path="/support"
>
  <PageHero
    title="Use Sift with a clear picture and a careful question."
    description="Get better scan results, understand what Sift can and cannot tell you, and find help when something does not look right."
    compact
  />

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Three habits for a more useful scan</h2>
        <p>A scan starts with the information Sift can see. A few deliberate choices make that information easier to review.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h2>Check the profile first</h2>
          <p>
            Confirm the correct person's allergens, severity, notes, and cross-contact preferences before scanning.
            A profile guides the review, but it cannot make an incomplete menu complete.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h2>Photograph readable sections</h2>
          <p>
            Hold the camera steady in even light. Avoid glare, deep shadows, steep angles, folded pages, and tiny
            text. For a long menu, scan one readable section at a time.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h2>Include the full description</h2>
          <p>
            Capture the dish name and its complete printed description together. Sauces, garnishes, sides, broths,
            and preparation notes often appear away from the main ingredient.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="principle-card">
          <h2>Finish with staff confirmation</h2>
          <p>
            Use Sift's questions to ask about ingredients, substitutions, shared equipment, fryers, and preparation.
            A result without a flagged concern is not proof that a dish is safe.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section--tint">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>If a scan looks wrong or incomplete</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Do not rely on the result to make a food-safety decision.</li>
        <li>Check that the correct allergy profile and restaurant language are selected.</li>
        <li>Retake the image closer to the menu, with the text flat, sharp, and evenly lit.</li>
        <li>Try a smaller menu section so each dish name and description is readable.</li>
        <li>Ask restaurant staff directly if the menu still leaves an ingredient or preparation question unresolved.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        If the problem repeats, email <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a> with the app
        version, device model, and a description of the steps you took. Remove personal and health information from
        screenshots before attaching them.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Your information on this device</h2>
        <p>Sift is local-first, but a requested menu analysis still requires processing beyond your device.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Allergy profiles, onboarding choices, language preferences, and scan history are stored on your device.
          You can edit or delete profiles and clear local scan history in the app. Clearing app data or uninstalling
          Sift can remove local information, and it may not be recoverable afterward.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you choose to analyze a menu, the selected menu image, relevant allergy profile details, language
          preference, and basic request information may be sent to Sift's analysis service and an AI provider to
          produce the requested result. Sift does not use menu photos for advertising tracking.
        </p>
        <p>
          Read the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for processing, retention, choices, and contact details. If
          account features are enabled for you, see <a href="/delete-account">Delete your account</a> for deletion
          options.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section--tint" id="faq">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <p>Direct answers to the questions that matter most before using a scan at the table.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-grid">
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h2>Does Sift tell me a dish is safe?</h2>
          <p>
            No. Sift cannot verify a complete recipe, substitutions, supplier changes, preparation surfaces, shared
            fryers, staff practices, or cross-contact. Confirm with restaurant staff before ordering.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h2>What does “possible concern” mean?</h2>
          <p>
            Sift found visible menu language or a common ingredient pattern that may relate to the selected profile.
            It is a prompt to inspect the explanation and ask staff—not a diagnosis or confirmed ingredient list.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h2>What does “unclear” mean?</h2>
          <p>
            The image, menu text, or available ingredient information was not clear enough for a useful conclusion.
            Retake the photo or ask staff directly rather than treating an unclear result as low risk.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h2>Can Sift detect cross-contact?</h2>
          <p>
            It can recognize menu wording and preparation patterns that suggest a question, but it cannot see the
            kitchen. Ask about shared equipment, utensils, surfaces, oil, storage, and preparation procedures.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h2>Why might Sift miss an allergen?</h2>
          <p>
            Menus can omit ingredients, use unfamiliar names, change without notice, or be difficult to read. Image
            quality and language can also affect the result. An unflagged item has not been verified as safe.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h2>Can I manage a profile for someone I care for?</h2>
          <p>
            Yes. Sift supports multiple profiles for diners and caregivers. Keep each profile current, and confirm
            the person's care plan and allergy details with them, their guardian, or a qualified healthcare
            professional as appropriate.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h2>Can I use a translated restaurant message?</h2>
          <p>
            Use it as a conversation aid, not as a verified translation. Automated translations can be incomplete or
            wrong. Confirm important allergy and preparation details with a fluent speaker or restaurant staff when
            possible.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h2>Can I scan a menu from my photo library?</h2>
          <p>
            Yes. Choose Upload Photo and select the menu image you want reviewed. Sift accesses the selected image
            for that request; it does not need your photo library for unrelated purposes.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h2>How do I remove local information?</h2>
          <p>
            Edit or delete allergy profiles and clear scan history in the app. Uninstalling Sift or clearing its app
            data can also remove local information. Review the Privacy Policy before acting if you need to keep a
            record.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h2>What should I do during an allergic reaction?</h2>
          <p>
            Do not use Sift or email support for emergency help. Contact local emergency services and follow the
            emergency plan provided by your healthcare professional.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>Still need help?</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>. Tell us what screen you were on, what
        you expected, and what happened instead.
      </p>
      <div class="callout callout--warning">
        <strong>Do not send sensitive health information or unredacted allergy profile details unless support asks for specific information and explains why it is needed.</strong>
      </div>
      <p>Sift support is not a restaurant verification, medical advice, or emergency service.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
